{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (PATIENT): I am sorry we are late, Doctor. The robot by the garage was out, and the traffic was really hectic.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ag, shame, don't apologise. Come in and sit, both of you. I'm just glad you made it through.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): We left the flat in good time, hey. Then the parking queue ate the whole morning.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ja, Mondays are like that. So, tell me, what's been worrying you?",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (PATIENT): Thank you, Doctor. I have come about a lump in my neck.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mm. Talk me through it, in your own time.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (PATIENT): It is on the left side, just under the jaw. I noticed it, uh, two weeks ago... no, three weeks ago. I miscounted, I apologise.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): No stress. Does it hurt, or is it sore when you touch it?",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (PATIENT): No, Doctor. It is not painful at all.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I saw it when she was tying her hair for work. And she sleeps badly, tossing half the night.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (PATIENT): With respect, that is not correct. I sleep well. I have not been up in the night.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Alright. You feel your sleep is fine, and your mom has seen something else, so we'll leave that open. Have you had a fever?",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (PATIENT): No, Doctor, no fever now, and none in these weeks. I did have night sweats once, a single night, and then it stopped.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): Just the once, hey. Any loss of weight? Any cough, or a sore throat?",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (PATIENT): No loss of weight. No cough, and my throat is not sore.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): And your stomach? Any nausea, pain, or diarrhoea?",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (PATIENT): No. My stomach has been perfectly fine, thank you.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (PATIENT): I should mention, the nurse in the passage checked me earlier. She said my blood pressure was one eighteen over seventy four.",
  "[SEG0019] person_4 (NURSE): Sorry to butt in, Doctor. Ja, blood pressure is 118 over 74, heart rate 76, temperature thirty six point seven, sats 98 percent on air, respiratory rate 16.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Thanks, Sister, that's grand. Any other lumps, under the arms or in the groin?",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (PATIENT): No, Doctor. Only this one in the neck.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. Any pets at home, or a scratch or a bite in the last while?",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (PATIENT): We have a cat. She scratched my left forearm. Umm, I cannot say which day it was. I am not certain.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The cut healed in five days. Small scratch, closed nicely, no pus or anything.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): So it healed in the normal time? Not a wound that was slow to close?",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (PATIENT): Yes, Doctor. It healed normally. There was no slow healing.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (DOCTOR): Are you taking any medicines at the moment?",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (PATIENT): Yes. Ferrus sulphate, for low iron. The dose is, err, sixty five milligrams... no, sorry, two hundred milligrams, once a day by mouth.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She does not take the tablets on Sundays. I check the pill box.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (PATIENT): Ah, that is not Sundays. I skip them on Saturdays, not Sundays. The other days I take the tablet.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (DOCTOR): Okay, so two hundred milligrams, and you miss Saturdays. How long has the iron been going?",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (PATIENT): About four months. The low iron is still being treated. I have no other conditions.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any operations in the past?",
  "[SEG0034] person_1 (PATIENT): No, none at all.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any allergies to medicines, or to anything else?",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (PATIENT): No. I have no allergies.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Her uncle, my brother, had tuberculosis, years back. I thought you should know.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (DOCTOR): Thank you, that helps. Do you smoke, or take alcohol?",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (PATIENT): I have never smoked. I drink very little, perhaps a glass of wine at a braai, not every week.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (DOCTOR): And work? Who is at home with you?",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (PATIENT): I work as a junior accountant. I live with my mother, and we have the cat.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (DOCTOR): Lovely. May I have a feel of the neck? Just turn a little toward the window.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (PATIENT): Of course, Doctor.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (DOCTOR): There's a firm mobile node on the left side of the neck, about two centimetres. It is not tender, and the skin is not red. I can't feel other nodes in the neck, the axillae or the groin. Your throat looks clear.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (DOCTOR): My impression is this is most likely a reactive lymph node. I can't exclude cat scratch disease, given that scratch, so that stays on the list.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'd like blood tests today, a full blood count and a CRP, and reception will book an ultrasound of the neck. We might do a chest X-ray if the bloods or the node do not settle, but not for now. Come back and see me in two weeks with the results. If the lump grows quickly or you get a fever, please come sooner rather than waiting."
 ],
